[b]Split up your boys in two teams and do a drill battle — on land, at sea (War Sails), or a siege drill on your own walls, castle or town.
Pick your battleground (and time) before the drills — and before the real battles.[/b]

[h1]Looking for…?[/h1]

If one of these searches brought you here — yes, this is that mod:
[list]
[*]a mod for [b]practice battles[/b] / [b]sparring[/b] — train your troops with no losses (deaths near zero, can be turned fully off)
[*]a mod for [b]naval training battles[/b] / practice [b]sea battles[/b] with your own fleet (War Sails)
[*]a mod for [b]siege practice[/b] — storm or defend [b]your own castle or town walls[/b] in a mock siege
[*]a mod to [b]change the time of day of battles[/b] — fight at [b]full bright daylight[/b], night, dawn, noon or evening
[*]a mod to [b]pick the battlefield[/b] / [b]choose where you fight[/b] before a battle
[*]a mod to [b]scout the battlefield before the battle[/b] — walk it on foot, see the real deployment lines
[*]a mod to [b]preview the deployment[/b] before committing to an attack
[*]a mod to [b]free sail your ship[/b] — take the [b]flagship[/b] out with your crew and scout the sea lanes (War Sails)
[/list]

A mod built on two pillars:

[h1]Pillar 1 — Training battles[/h1]

Press [b]G[/b] on the campaign map to open the muster.
[list]
[*][b]Split your army[/b] into two halves through a troop-picking screen, choose which half you command
[*][b]At sea too (War Sails)[/b] — the fleet divides with the men (your flagship stays yours), or divide it [b]at your word[/b] through the ship-divide window. Every hull comes back afterward: sunk, damaged or captured, training costs no ships
[*][b]Pay[/b] for the drill — broken javelins, arrows, rewards, they cost money… (1 daily wage by default, 2 at sea)
[*][b]Choose your side[/b] — attack or defend — then [b]fight[/b] the battle yourself or send the men in and watch it resolve from the hill
[*][b]Level up[/b] your soldiers — keep a share of the XP, scaled by your [b]Quartermaster[/b] (the [b]First Mate[/b] at sea); a great one even earns bonus XP
[*]The [b]KIA[/b] → most get back up; a few wake up wounded, and in unlucky cases a man truly dies — a good [b]Surgeon[/b] helps a lot (deaths can be turned fully off)
[*]The [b]wounded[/b] → they get up OK; a few may stay wounded, the surgeon again
[*][b]No loot[/b] — nothing is looted in sparring (works even alongside loot mods like BannerLoot)
[*][b]Disorganized[/b] after — they had to form up etc.
[*][b]Cooldown[/b] — you have to wait before the next drill (24 in-game hours by default)
[/list]

[b]Mock enemy[/b] [i](on by default, can be turned off)[/i] — compose a phantom force from [b]every troop in the game[/b], any cultures, any mix — and drill the whole company against it. The phantoms never touch your roster and vanish afterward. At sea they [b]sail[/b]: lay down their fleet from any culture's hulls, and it vanishes with them.

[b]Siege drills — castles and towns[/b] — at your [b]own castle or town[/b] (its own option on the settlement menu) the muster becomes a [b]siege drill[/b]: storm your own walls or hold them, on the real scene at its true wall level. The [b]garrison and militia[/b] stand with the defense, your [b]Engineer[/b] readies the siege equipment for both sides, and the same training rules cover everyone. A grand muster costs more, keeps a per-stronghold clock, and earns a little [b]renown and influence[/b]. Storm a town whose defenders pull back in good order and the [b]Lord's Hall[/b] waits — pick your best few and finish the drill in the keep, or let them stand. The mock enemy comes to the walls too: phantoms besiege you when you hold, reinforce the garrison when you storm.

[h1]Pillar 2 — Scouting & choosing your ground[/h1]

What a real general does before the battle: know the field — and pick the hour.
[list]
[*][b]Choose the time of day[/b] — morning, noon, afternoon, evening, night, or the campaign clock (default) — for drills, real field battles, sieges and sea battles alike
[*][b]Select the battlefield[/b] — the map patch's own scene (marked [i]"this ground"[/i]) plus every scene of the local terrain type
[*][b]Ride out and scout[/b] — walk any of those battlefields [b]alone[/b]: no battle, no cost, no cooldown. You spawn on your deployment line, facing the enemy's
[*][b]Scout the sea too (War Sails)[/b] — afloat, the same option takes your [b]flagship[/b] out: you and your crew alone on the chosen water, and the hull comes home without a scratch. A free sail, by design
[*][b]Scouted lines = drilled lines[/b] — drills use the same deterministic deployment as the scout, so what you scouted is what you get
[*][b]Same tools in REAL battles[/b] [i](per-side toggles, both on by default)[/i] — the encounter menu offers the hour, the scout and the battlefield pick when defending [b]or[/b] attacking; both armies stand frozen, so the scouted lines and facings are [b]exact[/b]
[*][b]Out-scout to earn it[/b] — in a real battle, the ground or a non-daylight hour must be earned: your [b]Scout[/b] against the enemy's best (the [b]Navigator[/b] at sea). The campaign clock and full daylight are always free
[/list]

[h1]Your companions matter[/h1]

The drill yard runs on your officers:
[list]
[*][b]Quartermaster[/b] [i](the [b]First Mate[/b] at sea)[/i] — sets the share of XP the men keep; a great one even earns bonus XP
[*][b]Your skilled fighters[/b] — the best fighter companions instruct on the yard, adding to the XP kept
[*][b]Steward[/b] — a well-run camp: shortens the wait for the next drill
[*][b]Surgeon[/b] — fewer real deaths among the fallen, fewer men who stay wounded
[*][b]Engineer[/b] — higher Engineering unlocks heavier siege equipment for the wall drills
[*][b]Scout[/b] [i](the [b]Navigator[/b] at sea)[/i] — out-scouting the enemy unlocks the battlefield and hour picks in real battles
[/list]

[h1]The knobs[/h1]

Every parameter lives in a JSON config ([i]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\TrainingBattles\config.json[/i]) [b]and[/b] in the in-game [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu (MCM)[/url] — a soft dependency; the config file alone runs the show without it. Each officer has its own group of sliders, with the drill pay, cooldowns, castle and town rates, time-of-day and every toggle beside them.

[h1]The road ahead[/h1]

Next milestone: [b]army training[/b] — drill a hosted [b]army[/b] against a mock enemy. No dates promised — this is a hobby, and playtesting sets the pace.

[h1]Safe & compatible[/h1]

[list]
[*]A training battle never silently costs you: no ships lost, no prisoner loss, no loot loss, no relation or crime side effects — the only real cost is the small death chance above, and it can be set to 0
[*]War Sails is [b]optional[/b] — without the DLC everything works on land as before
[*]Cancel is always available before the fight starts and leaves the campaign exactly as it was
[*]No Harmony patches — the mod rides vanilla's own model chain, so it stacks politely with other mods
[*]Safe to add to an existing save; when removing, finish (or cancel) any running drill first
[/list]

